# Notification System Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines establish patterns for implementing a reliable notification system across all platforms. While specific implementations may vary by platform, the core principles should be consistent.

## Best Practices
- Implement platform-specific notification handling
- Design proper notification grouping and categorization
- Support deep linking from notifications to specific app content
- Implement proper notification permission handling
- Design user-configurable notification settings
- Support different notification types (message, group, system)
- Implement notification action buttons where appropriate
- Design proper notification persistence and retrieval
- Support notification read/unread status tracking
- Implement proper notification analytics
- Design battery-efficient background notification handling

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- Organize notification-related components:
  ```
  lib/
    core/
      notifications/
        notification_manager.dart
        notification_handler.dart
        notification_channel.dart
        notification_payload.dart
        platform/
          android_notification_service.dart
          ios_notification_service.dart
          web_notification_service.dart
    data/
      repositories/
        notification_repository_impl.dart
      datasources/
        notification_local_datasource.dart
        notification_remote_datasource.dart
    domain/
      repositories/
        notification_repository.dart
      entities/
        app_notification.dart
      usecases/
        handle_notification_usecase.dart
        update_notification_settings_usecase.dart
    presentation/
      screens/
        notification_settings_screen.dart
      widgets/
        notification_list_item.dart
  ```

## Coding & Styling Conventions
- Use enum for notification types: `NotificationType.message`, `NotificationType.system`
- Implement standardized notification payload structure
- Use factory methods for creating platform-specific handlers
- Follow consistent naming for notification operations
- Define clear notification priority levels
- Implement proper error handling for notification operations
- Document platform-specific limitations

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Implement selective notification loading and pagination
- Batch notification operations when possible
- Optimize notification payload size
- Implement efficient background notification processing
- Use proper notification channels/categories by platform
- Implement notification throttling for high-frequency events
- Design efficient notification storage and retrieval
- Minimize wake-ups for background notification processing
- Implement proper cleanup for old notifications
- Use Firebase FCM best practices for push notifications

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Test notifications across all supported platforms
- Verify deep linking functionality
- Test notification actions and responses
- Validate notification appearance and styling
- Test notifications with different permission settings
- Verify notification grouping and categorization
- Test notification behavior in different app states (foreground, background, terminated)
- Validate notification throttling and batching
- Test notification performance with high volumes
- Implement notification delivery monitoring
- Test notification storage and retrieval efficiency